    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0540" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.74/990: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-10T20:00:00-04:00">July 10, 1943—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1010. Your 1481, July 3, 1943. The British Government is about to place an
                    embargo on all cipher telegrams filed by Axis missions with <pb facs="0541"
                        n="529" xml:id="pg529"/> telegraph companies under British control for
                    transmission by cable. The British have asked us whether we will take similar
                    action with regard to United States companies.</p>
                <p>Before taking similar action with regard to the I. T. &amp; T. cable from Buenos
                    Aires to Rio de Janeiro, the Department wishes your views with regard to
                    possible reactions in Argentina.</p>
                <p>The Department is instructing the Embassy in Rio to ascertain whether the
                    Brazilian authorities will be willing to forbid the transmission of all messages
                    in code over its international radio circuits.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
